  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: JxPath\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: JxPath\n       Program: commons-jxpath\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/JxPath/JxPath.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-jxpath.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/JxPath/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 22\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: JxPath-17\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\na1bc20f2af31730caa12faa116e14a964354f28d\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2008-02-03 02:13:59 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nJXPATH-109\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/JXPATH-109\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMModelTest::testAxisAttribute\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: Evaluating value iterator <vendor/product/price:amount/@*> expected:<[10%, 20%]> but was:<[20%]>\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.jdom.JDOMModelTest::testAxisAttribute\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError: Evaluating value iterator <vendor/product/price:amount/@*> expected:<[10%, 20%]> but was:<[20%]>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMAttributeIterator\n - org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.jdom.JDOMAttributeIterator\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: Namespaced attribute not selected with wildcard\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Resolved | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nWith expression:\n\nxml/@*\n\nOn xml:\n\n<xml xmlns:x='foo' x:pop='a'/>\n\nselectSingleNode returns null, @x:* works fine.\n\nPossible Fix:\n\nIn DOMAttributeIterator, line 84\n\nif (equalStrings(testPrefix, nodePrefix)) {\n                return true;\n            }\n\nshould probably be changed to\n\nif (testPrefix==null || equalStrings(testPrefix, nodePrefix)) {\n                return true;\n            }\n\nComments:\n\n[Michele Vivoda]: Making the change as suggeste breaks one test, that in my opinion is wrong.\n\nLine 543 of XMLModelTestCase\n\n        // attribute:: with default namespace and wildcard\n        assertXPathValueIterator(\n            context,\n            \"vendor/product/price:amount/@*\",\n            list(\"20%\"));\n\nA wildcard attribute selects all the attributes with or without a namespace, \nand not as is written, attributes with default namespace.\n\nSo I believe it should be changed to :\n\n        // attribute:: with no namespace\n        assertXPathValueIterator(\n            context,\n            \"vendor/product/price:amount/@*[namespace-uri()='']\",\n            list(\"20%\"));\n\n       // attribute::  all\n        assertXPathValueIterator(\n            context,\n            \"vendor/product/price:amount/@*\",\n            set(\"10%\", \"20%\"));\n\nmust also add to JXPathTestCase:\n\nprotected static Set set(Object o1, Object o2) {\n        Set list = new HashSet();\n        list.add(o1);\n        list.add(o2);\n        return list;\n    }\n\nRunning the test I noticed also JDOM model is affected by the same problem,\nso at line 82 of JDOMAttributeIterator:\n\nif (attr.getNamespace().equals(ns)) {\n                        attributes.add(attr);\n}\n\nshould become:\n\nif (prefix==null || attr.getNamespace().equals(ns)) {\n                        attributes.add(attr);\n}\n\nWith this last change tests run ok.\n\n[Matthew Jason Benson]: fixed; rev 617940",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMAttributeIterator (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.dom.DOMAttributeIterator (fixed)\n@@ -81,18 +81,14 @@\n         if (testLocalName.equals(\"*\") || testLocalName.equals(nodeLocalName)) {\n             String testPrefix = name.getPrefix();\n \n-            if (equalStrings(testPrefix, nodePrefix)) {\n+            if (testPrefix == null || equalStrings(testPrefix, nodePrefix)) {\n                 return true;\n             }\n-            String testNS = null;\n-            if (testPrefix != null) {\n-                testNS = parent.getNamespaceURI(testPrefix);\n+            if (nodePrefix == null) {\n+                return false;\n             }\n-            String nodeNS = null;\n-            if (nodePrefix != null) {\n-                nodeNS = parent.getNamespaceURI(nodePrefix);\n-            }\n-            return equalStrings(testNS, nodeNS);\n+            return equalStrings(parent.getNamespaceURI(testPrefix), parent\n+                    .getNamespaceURI(nodePrefix));\n         }\n         return false;\n     }\n@@ -152,4 +148,4 @@\n         this.position = position;\n         return position >= 1 && position <= attributes.size();\n     }\n-}\n+}\n--- org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.jdom.JDOMAttributeIterator (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.model.jdom.JDOMAttributeIterator (fixed)\n@@ -67,11 +67,9 @@\n             String lname = name.getName();\n             if (!lname.equals(\"*\")) {\n                 attributes = new ArrayList();\n-                if (ns != null) {\n                 Attribute attr = element.getAttribute(lname, ns);\n                 if (attr != null) {\n                     attributes.add(attr);\n-                    }\n                 }\n             }\n             else {\n@@ -79,7 +77,8 @@\n                 List allAttributes = element.getAttributes();\n                 for (int i = 0; i < allAttributes.size(); i++) {\n                     Attribute attr = (Attribute) allAttributes.get(i);\n-                    if (attr.getNamespace().equals(ns)) {\n+                    if (ns == Namespace.NO_NAMESPACE\n+                            || attr.getNamespace().equals(ns)) {\n                         attributes.add(attr);\n                     }\n                 }\n@@ -114,4 +113,4 @@\n         this.position = position;\n         return position >= 1 && position <= attributes.size();\n     }\n-}\n+}"
